<section class="section"><div class="container detail-grid"><article><p class="eyebrow">PROJECT-BASED ASSESSMENT</p><h2>Every learner should leave with something they have built.</h2><p>SkillsPark uses practical projects to help learners apply what they have learned, demonstrate progress and build confidence through real work. In graphic design, learners complete final project work that becomes part of their assessment record before course completion and certificate eligibility.</p></article><article><p class="eyebrow">From script to final edit</p><h2>Video becomes practical when the full process is understood.</h2><p>Video-editing learners work through the wider production process, from planning and scripting to production and final post-production. By the final stage, learners bring footage, sound and visual elements together into a completed video using the editing skills developed during training.</p></article></div></section>
